    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Glossary index in urn:stdo:bounded-context:graph-native-odd, declared by ODD §1: ODD/Outcome-Driven Development, GTL/Graph Transformation Language and ABG have their owning clause at ODD §1; ABG also has the ODD abg relation clause. Edge Traversal/Traversal is owned at ODD traversal; Probabilistic Compute, F_D, F_P and F_H at ODD probabilistic-compute; F_P and F_H additionally route to SPEC_METHOD §5. Closure decisions are close, yield, retry(defeated), retry(undecided), repair(implementation), repair(proof), re-enter(undeclared), re-enter(basis), reprice, block(undeclared), block(basis), owned at ODD §11.5D. Audit outcomes are compliant, non-compliant, valid and worth incorporating, owned at ODD §9. Both result rows route to FOUNDATIONS Results.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":300,
          "quote":"Context declared by [ODD §1](ODD.md#1-position) (P3). `F_D`, `F_P` and\n`F_H` are also indexed in the axiomatic-calculus context in §4; the two\nrows create no identity between the contexts (P1).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F14.%20Graph-native%20ODD",
