    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Nodes are durable truth surfaces or product assets, each naming a bounded state of truth. Illustrative software-development names are intent, product, requirements, design, module_decomp, code, uat_testcases, integration_tests, bootloader and build targets; these names are product-local rather than mandatory universal names.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":288,
          "quote":"Nodes are durable truth surfaces or product assets; each names a bounded\nstate of truth. In one software-development ODD product the nodes include\n`intent`, `product`, `requirements`, `design`, `module_decomp`, `code`,\n`uat_testcases`, `integration_tests`, `bootloader` and build targets. Those\nnames are illustrative and product-local; the law is that nodes name\nbounded states (P3).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FNodes",
