      ],
      "key":"odd_traversal_workflow",
      "label":"ODD traversal workflow"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The installed graph-native product provides method, runtime, carrier/control/command surfaces, release-managed methodology and scaffold templates. The distinct target project owns one stdo_<label>.json per distinct Product WHAT, locating constitutional, local/collective reference-frame basis, realisation, work and composition surfaces; its constitutional surfaces; one or more realisation roots bound through how.build_tenants; its domain outputs/evidence. Software examples are GOALS.md, INTENT.md, PRODUCT.md, requirements/, build_tenants/, design/code/tests/documents/proof; these scaffold names are defaults. A clean install is described as installation, authoring target intent/definition/requirements/realisation root, then graph traversal to produce target domain outputs.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":419,
          "quote":"The graph-native product and the project built with it are distinct. The\ninstalled product provides the method, the runtime and the carrier\nsurfaces; it does not provide the target project's business domain. The\ninstalled product must not assume prior knowledge of the target project's\ndomain (P6, P3).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F6.%20Product%20boundary",
          "start_line":415
        },
        {
          "end_line":443,
          "quote":"- one `stdo_<label>.json` definition for each distinct product WHAT,\n  locating its constitutional, local and collective reference-frame\n  basis, realisation, work and composition surfaces;\n- its constitutional surfaces under SPEC_METHOD, where `GOALS.md`,\n  `INTENT.md`, `PRODUCT.md` and `requirements/` are the default\n  software-development scaffold and not mandatory names;\n- one or more realisation roots bound through `how.build_tenants`, where\n  `build_tenants/` is the default root name for software-development ODD\n  products and existing projects and other domain types may use their own\n  locations;",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F6.%20Product%20boundary",
          "start_line":434
        }
      ],
      "key":"installed_product_target_split",
      "label":"Installed product and target project"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A responsibility layer expresses a capability class bound by the product to local domain semantics, with GTL publishing lawful transitions. Illustrative classes are bootstrap/intake, design, implementation, qualification, release, operational transition and retrofit. They are not universal instance names.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":474,
          "quote":"This profile governs structural responsibility layers and their required\npublication shape. It does not freeze one product's local asset names as\nuniversal ODD doctrine. A responsibility layer expresses one capability\nclass; the product binds that capability to its own local domain\nsemantics; the GTL carrier publishes the lawful transitions for that bound\ncapability (P1, P3).\n\nCapability classes may include bootstrap or intake, design,\nimplementation, qualification, release, operational transition and\nretrofit. They are responsibility-layer ideas, not mandatory universal\ninstance names (P1).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F8.%20Responsibility%20layers%20and%20local%20binding",
          "start_line":464
        }
      ],
      "key":"odd_responsibility_layer",
      "label":"ODD responsibility layer"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Audit of a move against the current ODD profile has three outcomes for the predicate 'the move complies with the current profile': compliant maps to satisfied because the move meets current law; non-compliant maps to falsified with the violated law as counterexample; valid and worth incorporating maps to out_of_frame because needed law is undeclared, naming that law, this profile as owner and the required update. Incorporation is neither compliance nor failure.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":529,
          "quote":"| compliant | satisfied | the move meets the law of the current profile |\n| non-compliant | falsified | the law of this profile that the move violates is the counterexample |\n| valid and worth incorporating | out_of_frame | the current profile does not declare the law the move needs; the outcome names that law, this profile as its owner and the update it requires, which is the reconfiguration pressure of out_of_frame ([FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), Out of frame or indeterminate) |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F9.%20Method%20governance%20and%20audit",
