      "definition": "An ODD product is a configured GTL/ABG domain product whose constructive work uses published graph functions over typed assets. Its ten-part application boundary comprises Bootstrap Surface, Initialization Surface, Domain Configuration, Typed Domain Assets/Nodes, GTL Function Catalog, GTL Module, Policy Hook Bindings, ABG Runtime, Projection/Query Surface and Proof Surface. Universal ownership is one WHAT surface, one HOW relation, ABG-owned runtime and Product-owned domain meaning; actual locations are bound by the product definition.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":554,
          "quote":"App\n= Bootstrap Surface\n+ Initialization Surface\n+ Domain Configuration\n+ Typed Domain Assets / Nodes\n+ GTL Function Catalog\n+ GTL Module\n+ Policy Hook Bindings\n+ ABG Runtime\n+ Projection / Query Surface\n+ Proof Surface\n```",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is",
          "start_line":543
